      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. The original class contains many unused helper methods (`charsetSanityCheck`, `testCharset`, `getByteBufferUtf8`, `log`, etc.) and imports that clutter the file. The actual test logic is simple but benefits from a brief explanation of the non-obvious ByteBuffer window setup. I'll produce a cleaned-up version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all unused helper methods and imports, keeping only the single `@Test` method and the `allocate` helper it needs, with brief comments explaining the non-obvious ByteBuffer window setup (`position=1, limit=2`) and the meaning of the `true` flag."
